  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Cynergy Professional Systems obligated $252M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Cynergy Professional Systems received 269 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $936K, and obligations are up 248.2% year over year. Cynergy Professional Systems shows concentration in a small number of agencies. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $102M and the Department of Justice obligated $76.7M. Cynergy Professional Systems also did work for the Department of Veterans Affairs, which obligated $44.4M. Cynergy Professional Systems is concentrated by market. Other Computer Related Services accounts for $236M of obligations, while the next largest market is Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $5.6M. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity, and award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables would be total contract values where those tables are provided.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is the main buyer, with obligations of $102M. The Department of Justice follows with obligations of $76.7M, and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $44.4M. Several other agencies obligated smaller amounts, including the Department of Defense at $5.9M and the General Services Administration at $5.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which NAICS markets account for the work?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the dominant market, accounting for $236M of obligations. Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing accounts for $5.6M. Additional markets include Computer Systems Design Services and Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths), each at $2.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
